Note, a tick loop that counts upwards and stops on its own.
Note, ticks are driven by the window, so the program stays alive by itself.

Open window with title Ticker.
Add canvas board with width 300 and height 120.

Let count be 0.

Every 200 milliseconds, do the following.
Add 1 to count.
Clear canvas.
Draw text the value of count at 150 by 60 with color white.
Say the value of count.
If the value of count is greater than 9, do the following.
Say Done counting.
Stop ticking.
End if.
End every.
